The  driver provides kernel support for hardware‐accelerated vir‐
tualization.  It is made of a generic MI frontend,  to  which  MD
backends can be plugged to implement the core virtualization.  In
practice,  is used by the API to implement hypervisors.  The fol‐
lowing backends are supported: x86‐SVM, for x86 AMD CPUs x86‐VMX,
